Experiment 1a:Sort in Ascending Order

Aim:
To write a Java program to sort the given array elements in ascending order.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Declare and initialize an integer array.
3. Compare each element with the next element.
4. Swap the elements if they are in the wrong order.
5. Display the array in ascending order.
6. Stop the program

Program:
Ascending Order in Java

import java.util.Scanner;

public class AscendingOrder {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int a[] = {50, 20, 40, 10, 30};
        int temp;

        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j < a.length; j++) {
                if (a[i] > a[j]) {
                    temp = a[i];
                    a[i] = a[j];
                    a[j] = temp;
                }
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Ascending Order:");
        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {
            System.out.print(a[i] + " ");
        }
    }
}

Output:

Ascending Order:
10 20 30 40 50

Result:
Thus, the Java program to sort the given array elements in ascending order was executed successfully.
